            <h2>Dataset Overview & Historical Context</h2>
            <p>
                The Academy Award for Best Original Score was first presented at the 7th ceremony in 1934,
                recognizing compositions created specifically for the film. This dataset spans 93 ceremonies
                from 1934 through 2026, encompassing the full history of the award through the 98th Academy Awards.
            </p>
            <p>
                The award has undergone several name changes and occasional subcategory splits (dramatic vs.
                comedy/musical scores), but this analysis consolidates to one winner per year. The data reveals
                77 distinct composers across nine decades, with notable clustering of wins among a small elite
                group of repeat winners.
            </p>
