                <div class="chart-title">Repeat Wins vs First-Time Winners by Decade</div>
                <canvas id="repeatChart" height="300"></canvas>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="era-analysis">
            <h2>Era-Based Analysis of Winning Scores</h2>
            <p>
                Grouping the data into four historical eras reveals distinct characterizations of each period,
                from the orchestral grandeur of Hollywood's Golden Age to the diverse sonic palettes of
                contemporary cinema.
            </p>

            <div class="era-grid">
                <div class="era-card golden">
                    <div class="era-title">The Golden Age</div>
                    <div class="era-years">1934 – 1960</div>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem;">
                        Defined by romantic, orchestral scores. Max Steiner established the template for
                        cinematic composition. Dimitri Tiomkin dominated with 4 wins, masterfully scoring
                        Westerns and epics. The era favored lush, directive leitmotifs.
                    </p>
